2025-06-03 20:46:17,368 ID: 449 INFO SYSTEM:  Command `read_sonarqube_docu` returned:  
**Zero should not be a possible denominator**  

If the denominator to a division or modulo operation is zero it would result in a fatal error.

When working with `double` or `float`, no fatal error will be raised, but it will lead to unusual result and should be avoided anyway.

This rule supports primitive `int`, `long`, `double`, `float` as well as `BigDecimal` and `BigInteger`.

Noncompliant Code Example
    
    
    void test_divide() {
      int z = 0;
      if (unknown()) {
        // ..
        z = 3;
      } else {
        // ..
      }
      z = 1 / z; // Noncompliant, possible division by zero
    }
    

Compliant Solution
    
    
    void test_divide() {
      int z = 0;
      if (unknown()) {
        // ..
        z = 3;
      } else {
        // ..
        z = 1;
      }
      z = 1 / z;
    }
    

See

  * [MITRE, CWE-369](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/369) \- Divide by zero 
  * [CERT, NUM02-J.](https://wiki.sei.cmu.edu/confluence/x/CTZGBQ) \- Ensure that division and remainder operations do not result in divide-by-zero errors 
  * [CERT, INT33-C.](https://wiki.sei.cmu.edu/confluence/x/ftYxBQ) \- Ensure that division and remainder operations do not result in divide-by-zero errors 
